sec.p:
Those 64 publications were carefully studied and based on the inclusion and exclusion criteria, further eliminations were carried out. The reasons leading to elimination of full-text studies were:
Pooled analyses, meta-analyses, systematic reviews (n = 6);
Commentaries and letters to the editor (n = 4);
Studies that were subset of previously published trials (n = 10);
Studies that were published in a different language apart from English (n = 4);
Repeated studies (n = 36).

The efficacy outcomes which were assessed:
Deep venous thrombosis (DVT);
Venous thromboembolism (VTE);
Pulmonary embolism (PE).

The safety outcomes which were assessed included:
Major bleeding;
Fatal bleeding;
Minor bleeding;
Bleeding in a critical organ;
Bleeding requiring blood transfusion.
